## Example input 1:
Pensé que era un buen momento => I thought it was a good time
Por fin se hacía realidad => It was finally coming true
Tanto oír hablar de tu silencio => After hearing so much about your silence
Dicen que te arrastra como el mar => They say it pulls you in like the sea

## Expected output 1:

[Pensé] que era un buen momento => [I thought] it was a good time
Pensé que [era] un buen momento => I thought [it was] a good time
Pensé que era [un] buen momento => I thought it was [a] good time
Pensé que era un [buen] momento => I thought it was a [good] time
Pensé que era un buen [momento] => moment, time

[Por fin] se hacía realidad => It was [finally] coming true
Por fin [se hacía] realidad => was getting, was becoming # original English had "It was ... coming", but we must select only consecutive words so I used a custom translation
Por fin se hacía [realidad] => reality # original English had "true", but reality is a better word translation in a word-for-word context

[Tanto] oír hablar de tu silencio => After hearing [so much] about your silence
Tanto [oír] hablar de tu silencio => After [hearing] so much about your silence
Tanto oír [hablar] de tu silencio => to speak # custom translation, as "oír hablar" is a phrase
Tanto oír hablar [de] tu silencio => After hearing so much [about] your silence
Tanto oír hablar de [tu] silencio => After hearing so much about [your] silence
Tanto oír hablar de tu [silencio] => After hearing so much about your [silence]

[Dicen] que te arrastra como el mar => [They say] it pulls you in like the sea
Dicen [que] te arrastra como el mar => that
Dicen que [te arrastra] como el mar => They say [it pulls you in] like the sea
Dicen que te arrastra [como] el mar => They say it pulls you in [like] the sea
Dicen que te arrastra como [el mar] => They say it pulls you in like [the sea]

## Example input 2:

Cuatro abrazos y un café => Four hugs and a coffee
Apenas me desperté => I just woke up
Y al mirarte recordé => And when I looked at you, I remembered
Que ya todo lo encontré => That I'd already found everything

## Expected output 2

[Cuatro] abrazos y un café => [Four] hugs and a coffee
Cuatro [abrazos] y un café => Four [hugs] and a coffee
Cuatro abrazos [y] un café => Four hugs [and] a coffee
Cuatro abrazos y [un] café => Four hugs and [a] coffee
Cuatro abrazos y un [café] => Four hugs and a [coffee]

[Apenas] me desperté => I [just] woke up
Apenas [me desperté] => I woke up # using custom translation because "just" was in the middle but we must select consecutive words

[Y] al mirarte recordé => [And] when I looked at you, I remembered
Y [al mirarte] recordé => upon looking at you # spanish compresses a lot of meaning into this phrase. The English version is too different so I used a custom translation
Y al mirarte [recordé] => And when I looked at you, [I remembered]

[Que] ya todo lo encontré => [That] I'd already found everything
Que [ya] todo lo encontré => That I'd [already] found everything
Que ya [todo] lo encontré => That I'd already found [everything]
Que ya todo [lo encontré] => That I'd already [found] everything # encontré actually means "I found" but since we must select consecutive words I selected the more meaningful "found"

## Example input 3:
Hola otra vez, ¿qué le vamos a hacer? => Hello again, what can we do?

## Expected output 3:
[Hola] otra vez, ¿qué le vamos a hacer? => [Hello] again, what can we do?
Hola [otra vez], ¿qué le vamos a hacer? => Hello [again], what can we do?
Hola otra vez, ¿[qué] le vamos a hacer? => Hello again, [what] can we do?
Hola otra vez, ¿qué le [vamos a] hacer? => we are going to
Hola otra vez, ¿qué le vamos a [hacer?] => do
Hola otra vez, ¿qué [le] vamos a hacer? => about it # The “le” here is a dative pronoun which functions as an ethical dative

